        {
          "from": "[t] (morpheme-final stop)",
          "to": "[d]",
          "note": "Morphologically conditioned intervocalic voicing in Nuer: morpheme-final /t/ is voiced to [d] in intervocalic position before a vowel-initial suffix. This voicing alternation is restricted to morpheme-final consonants — the same consonant in suffix-initial position does not undergo the change. Dental articulation [t̪, d̪] is common before front vowels."
        }
      ]
    },
